formal_core:
One early connector assumed a fixed FullTurn budget and a binary count $$N_{\rm FullTurn}(r)=2^r,$$ so that $$E_{\rm wave}^{\rm old}(r)=\frac{E_{\rm FullTurn}^{\rm old}}{2^r}.$$ Other early blocks simultaneously used $$\mathrm{Tick}^{\rm old}(r)=2^r\mathrm{Tick}^{\rm old}(0),$$ which implies $$\omega^{\rm old}(r)=\frac{\omega^{\rm old}(0)}{2^r}.$$ Thus the old bookkeeping produced the parallel structure $$\frac{E_{\rm wave}^{\rm old}(r)}{E_{\rm wave}^{\rm old}(0)}
=
\frac{\omega^{\rm old}(r)}{\omega^{\rm old}(0)}
=2^{-r}.$$

The source hierarchy itself already anticipated this discipline: $$\boxed{
\text{root primitives}
\longrightarrow
\text{trunk consequences}
\longrightarrow
\text{branch applications}
}$$ with the additional rule that a branch should not silently introduce a rule that has no traceable root.

The historical roots and the active ledger now support a cleaner picture than either document contained alone: $$\boxed{
\begin{array}{c}
\text{declared cyclic reference}\\[0.25em]
\Downarrow\\[0.25em]
\text{closure event}\\[0.25em]
\Downarrow\\[0.25em]
(\mathrm{Gam}_F,\mathrm{Tick}_F,\omega_F,E_F)\\[0.25em]
\Downarrow\\[0.25em]
\text{local dimensionless ratios}\\[0.25em]
\Downarrow\\[0.25em]
\text{cross-frame map with declared reference ownership}\\[0.25em]
\Downarrow\\[0.25em]
\text{frame-independent ratio only when common factors truly cancel}
\end{array}
}$$

This makes the recent zero/local discussion less mysterious. The current factor $D$ is not itself an angular velocity. It is the declared common stretch coefficient in the equal-stretch branch: $$D=\frac{\mathrm{Gam}_L}{\mathrm{Gam}_0}
=\frac{\mathrm{Tick}_L}{\mathrm{Tick}_0},$$ so $$\boxed{
\frac{\omega_L}{\omega_0}
=
\frac{E_L}{E_0}
=
\frac{1}{D}.
}$$ The old notebook contributes the operational reason to ask *whose* reference is being used; the active ledger supplies the corrected unit convention and the exact angular-energy dictionary.
